From 194748d96994f2ee7ed29408f70b1bc20e64b8ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialise the spatial tokenizer explicitly; refuse to
 pretrain uninitialised convs

Root cause of the dead pretrained map encoder (R9/R15): pretraining builds
the model with transformers' from_pretrained(None, config, state_dict=...).
Since transformers 4.31 that call wraps construction in no_init_weights(),
which replaces every torch.nn.init function with a no-op, and afterwards only
re-initialises modules covered by BERT's _init_weights (Linear, Embedding,
LayerNorm). nn.Conv2d is not covered, so a spatial_tokenizer absent from the
starting state_dict kept raw torch.empty memory: weight exactly zero (fresh
pages), bias arbitrary (norm 55 in checkpoint 387500, ~1e19 in 460000).
category_projection escaped because its weight is overwritten by an explicit
copy_ of CLIP embeddings; metadata_encoder got BERT's N(0, 0.02).

Reproduced with transformers 4.43.4 (the pinned version) on a toy
PreTrainedModel: from_pretrained(None, config, state_dict={}) leaves
conv.weight all zeros and conv.bias garbage (max 3.7e19), while a plain
constructor gives kaiming init.

- EmbeddingGridMapEncoder now initialises spatial_tokenizer with tensor-level
  uniform_ (not patched by no_init_weights), reproducing PyTorch's default.
- EmbeddingGridMapEncoder.assert_initialised() and
  train_r2r.assert_conv_modules_initialised() fail fast right after
  from_pretrained() if any conv parameter is all-zero or non-finite.
- Regression test builds the encoder inside no_init_weights() and checks the
  tokenizer is finite, bounded and non-zero.

